-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",466,{
[14881]="7007415B\n1\tDefeat wild mûmakil at Erakúndo ([see journal]/6)\030Defeat wild mûmakil bulls at Erakúndo ([see journal]/2)\tAt Erakúndo, wild mûmakil stamp the ground of the old lodes making their potential return to function improbable. The young will move if the bulls and mothers are destroyed. Do your best to not eradicate the herd by preserving the young. Help the dwarves of An Shêru drive out the mûmakil from Erakúndo. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[14882]="7007415C\n1\tDefeat roc huntresses at the Roost of Anzûri ([see journal]/10)\tThe Roost of the Anzûri is a place of ill-omen to the dwarves of An Shêru. Ancient lands, once fertile and lush are seized by rocs making the place their nests for raising their young. Rocs have been known to snatch pack animals used in trade, and the dwarves want the rocs' numbers thinned. Help the dwarves of An Shêru drive out the rocs from the Roost of the Anzûri.\n",
[14883]="70074168\n1\tDefeat serpents at Nax Shalâl ([see journal]/12)\tHorrors across Idagâl, be they of the mind and stirred spirits, or the physical pain wrought by man, should be addressed for the betterment of Mûr Ghala. Eliminate serpents at Nax Shalâl.\n",
[14884]="70074169\n1\tDefeat vultures at the Fane of Shahûru ([see journal]/12)\tHorrors across Idagâl, be they of the mind and stirred spirits, or the physical pain wrought by man, should be addressed for the betterment of Mûr Ghala. Eliminate vultures roosting at the Fane of Shahûru.\n",
[14885]="7007416A\n1\tDefeat gredbyg at Gnasher's Delf ([see journal]/12)\tHorrors across Idagâl, be they of the mind and stirred spirits, or the physical pain wrought by man, should be addressed for the betterment of Mûr Ghala. Eliminate gredbyg at Gnasher's Delf.\n",
[14886]="7007416C\n1\tExamine the unusual crate outside Mûl Erebu\tSomething bad seems to have happened at Mûl Erebu.\n2\tDefeat scorpions throughout Mûl Erebu (total: 6)\030Examine an unusual crate near the large tent in Mûl Erebu\030Examine an unusual crate near the back of Mûl Erebu\tYou should explore Mûl Erebu, defeating scorpions and learning what happened here.\n3\tExamine the Ordâkhai corpse in the back of Mûl Erebu\tA soldier of Ordâkh has been slain near the back of Mûl Erebu.\n4\tRead the Ordâkhai soldier's plan for the scorpions\tYou found a plan for the scorpions on the body of a slain Ordâkhai soldier.\n5\tBring the plan for scorpions to Zalûd the Maker of Plans at the war camp of Ingarûma\tZalûd the Maker of Plans at the war camp of Ingarûma will be very interested to learn what the Ordâkhai were up to in Mûl Erebu.\n",
[14887]="7007416D\n1\tCollect shoreline reeds for Unûza (total: 8)\tThe reeds Unûza requires can be found along the shoreline of the Hatokáli River.\n2\tBring shoreline reeds to Unûza in south-west Pahar Hatokáli\tUnûza is not far from the river in south-west Pahar Hatokáli.\n3\tBring Unûza's bandages to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of Ingarûma\tChief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma, and will appreciate the bandages.\n",
[14888]="7007416E\n1\tRetrieve stolen keepsakes from Orcs at Roz Káskrauz (total: 8)\tOrcs at Roz Káskrauz in north-east Pahar Hatokáli have stolen keepsakes from fallen Hamâti soldiers.\n2\tBring the stolen keepsakes to Nungíri outside Roz Káskrauz\tNungíri is outside Roz Káskrauz, waiting for you to return with the stolen keepsakes.\n",
[14889]="7007416F\n1\tScout the entrance to the palace in south-east Imizíla\030Scout the overlook in southern Imizíla\030Scout the entrance courtyard in northern Imizíla\030Defeat Ordâkhai within Imizíla (total: 12)\tOrdâkhai can be found throughout Imizíla, as can places of interest to Mizâdi's soldiers.\n2\tTalk to Takhsûl outside Imizíla\tTakhsûl is waiting outside Imizíla for your report.\n",
[14890]="70074172\n1\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story.\n2\tTalk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku\tLakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.\n3\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story.\n4\tTalk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku\tLakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.\n5\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story.\n6\tTalk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku\tLakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.\n7\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story.\n8\tTalk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku\tLakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.\n9\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story.\n10\tTalk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku\tLakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.\n11\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story\tLakhêpi is waiting to hear a story.\n12\tTalk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku\tLakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.\n",
[14891]="7007436A\n1\tComplete Mission: Orc-thieves\tYou have been asked to enter the Orc encampment at Bleakrift and recover Candaith's bow as well as any other stolen goods. Before leaving, you should defeat their leader, War-master Uzorr.\n2\tTalk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony\tYou have recovered Candaith's bow along with the other stolen goods and defeated the Orcs' leader, War-master Uzorr. You should talk to Candaith and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.\n",
[14892]="7007436B\n1\tCollect valuables from defeated War-singers (total: 8)\tCwendreda believes the War-singers carry the valuable treasures the Eglain need for trading. You should defeat them and search their remains for the valuables.\n2\tDefeat the Master of Nan Dhelu\tThe Master of Nan Dhelu is a fearsome wight that must be banished from the realm of the living. You should seek him out and defeat him.\n",
[14893]="7007436C\n1\tRecover Candaith's bow\030Collect battered lockboxes (total: 8)\030Defeat War-master Uzorr\tCandaith's pursuit of an Orc-company turned deadly when he was discovered, and in his haste to escape, he lost his bow to the Orcs. Search among the Orc-encampment at Bleakrift for anything else that may be of worth to the people of the Lone-lands, and defeat the chief of the Orc-thieves, War-master Uzorr.\n",
[14894]="7007436D\n1\tComplete Mission: Evil in the Ruins\tYou have been asked to defeat the Dead within the ruins of Nan Dhelu, including their master, and recover treasures of great value to the Eglain.\n2\tTalk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony\tYou have defeated many Dead within the ruins of Nan Dhelu, including their fearsome master, and recovered treasures of great value to the Eglain. You should talk to Cwendreda and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.\n",
[14895]="70074372\n1\tComplete Mission: The Orcs of Nan Wathren\tYou have been asked to go to the Orc camp in Nan Wathren and do what you can to disrupt the plans of Drukordh, their Uruk leader who intends to attack the Elven village Lin Giliath while it is vulnerable.\n2\tTalk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony\tYour strike on the Orcs of Nan Wathren has successfully brought an end to their plans to raid the Elven village of Lin Giliath. You should talk to Candaith and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.\n",
[14896]="70074373\n1\tComplete Mission: The Fortress of Olnathron\tYou have been asked to travel to the North Downs and enter the ruins of Tham Lorn in the Fields of Fornost. There you will face Olnathron, a fell-spirit that is a source of the evil stirrings that spread through these remnants of the once-glorious Kingdom of Arnor.\n2\tTalk to the Hooded Stranger in The Prancing Pony\tOlnathron has been sent back to the abyss. You should talk to Mincham and then give your report to the Hooded Stranger.\n",
[14897]="70074374\n1\tEnter the Orc camp\tYou are at the entrance to Nan Wathren. You should enter the encampment to disrupt the Orcs there.\n2\tDefeat the Tarkrîp pack-master\030Defeat Gloomfang\030Destroy corrupt altars (total: 5)\tThe Orcs at Nan Wathren seem to fear and respect the Tarkrîp Pack-master and someone called 'Gloomfang'. You should find and defeat them. They also appear to be bolstered by corrupt altars inside the camp. You should find and destroy them as well in order to disrupt their plans to attack the Elven village Lin Giliath.\n3\tDefeat Drukordh\tYou have brought disorder to the Orcs camped at Nan Wathren by defeating Gloomfang and the Tarkrîp pack-master and destroying their corrupt idols. You should now find and defeat Drukordh, the band's Uruk leader.\n",
[14898]="70074375\n1\tConfront the evil spirits of Tham Lorn\tEnter the ruins of Tham Lorn and confront the darkness within.\n2\tDisable burning idols (total: 6)\tStrange idols can be found all over Tham Lorn, spewing forth noxious green clouds. You must disable the idols and stop the spread of corruption from this evil place before confronting Olnathron.\n3\tDefeat the fell-spirit Olnathron\tWith the idols disabled, the path to Olnathron has been cleared. It is time to confront the fell-spirit once and for all.\n",
[14899]="700744DC\n1\tSabotage a well-built crate ([see journal]/6)\030Sabotage a well-built cage ([see journal]/6)\tYour efforts to slow the Ordâkhai incursion toward the overrun town west of their settlement has proven difficult. Mizâdi's scouts wish to change tactics. Sabotage the materials the Ordâkhai would use to contain and transport the scorpions.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tWith the crates and cages sabotaged, you are ready to return to the encampment. Search for Mizâdi's scout near where you arrived and return to safety.\n",
[14900]="700744DF\n1\tFind the bóro and retrieve the orders for soldiers\tFind the courier, a bóro descending from the Ordâkhai encampment within the crags to the south, but be cautious to not alert or be discovered by the forces guarding the pathways into the hills. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tReturn to the vale below without being detected\tYou recovered the orders from the courier. Make your way to the scout hidden in the vale below without being discovered. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tRetreat further down the hill and find Mizâdi's scout to return to her encampment.\n",
[14901]="700744E1\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai cat-handlers ([see journal]/12)\tCat-handlers among the Ordâkhai are capable of herding and controlling scorpions. Thinning their number will surely reduce the ability of the Ordâkhai forces to recover and use the scorpions against Mizâdi's forces.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tYou defeated the cat-handlers. Return to where you arrived and seek out the scout who will lead you back to the encampment.\n",
[14902]="700744E3\n1\tSearch for and defeat an Ordâkhai emissary\tMizâdi's scouts witnessed emissaries taking great care to not be seen making their way south toward a bandit encampment on the shore of the river to the south. You must not let the Ordâkhai enlist the bandits to their cause.\n2\tFind the second Ordâkhai emissary heading south near the road\tMizâdi's scouts witnessed emissaries taking great care to not be seen making their way south toward a bandit encampment on the shore of the river to the south. You must not let the Ordâkhai enlist the bandits to their cause.\n3\tFind a third Ordâkhai emissary heading south near the road\tMizâdi's scouts witnessed emissaries taking great care to not be seen making their way south toward a bandit encampment on the shore of the river to the south. You must not let the Ordâkhai enlist the bandits to their cause.\n4\tHide in the bushes east of the road near the bandit camp and observe\tMizâdi's scouts witnessed emissaries taking great care to not be seen making their way south toward a bandit encampment on the shore of the river to the south. You must not let the Ordâkhai enlist the bandits to their cause. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tWatch the exchange between the bandit and emissary\tObserve the exchange between the bandits and the Ordâkhai emissary. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tFind Mizâdi's scout north along the road\tYou were too late. An emissary reached the bandits. After a short discussion you could not hear, the emissary entered the bandit camp. You should return to Mizâdi's scout along the road to the north.\n",
[14903]="700744E5\n1\tBurn the empty crates ([see journal]/10)\tFind and destroy the crates at the area before the cross-roads. The Ordâkhai intend to use the crates to store and deliver the scorpions from the nearby town.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tFind Mizâdi's scout.\n",
[14904]="700744E6\n1\tDestroy the boats on the river-banks (total: 6)\tThe freed workers explained to Mizâdi's scouts that the forces you faced were looking to escape across the river into the jungle. Why? The workers do not know, but they were forced to build boats to cross the river. You can stop the enemy's escape.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe boats lie in ashes. Find Mizâdi's scout and return to her encampment.\n",
[14905]="700744E8\n1\tRecord your findings about the tools\tFind the Ordâkhai and Utûgi work-site to the west. Examine the tools they brought with them and record your findings before delivering them to back to the scouts.\n2\tDestroy the wooden planks ([see journal]/6)\tYou have recorded information about the tools in your journal. Now destroy the wooden planks so they cannot be used.\n3\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe planks are destroyed and the tools documented. Find Mizâdi's scout to return to the encampment.\n",
[14906]="700744E9\n1\tDefeat Khómabekh Dôlo\tYour procurement of the orders was translated and the identity of the dôlo in charge of the effort revealed. You must make your way to the village and thwart the machinations of the dôlo, before he corrals and recovers the scorpions.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe dôlo is defeated. The threat to Mizâdi's forces is diminished, for now. Return to the scout and the encampment to share the news.\n",
[14907]="700744EA\n1\tCollect the orders from the Ordâkhai bóro\tMizâdi's scouts learned that a new courier reached the encampment near the cross-roads. They believe the purpose, the method of recovery, and the leader spear-heading this effort are contained in the orders. You have been asked to recover the orders.\n2\tDeliver the orders to Mizâdi's scout\tYou have collected the orders. Find the scout and deliver the orders to them.\n",
[14908]="700744EC\n1\tBurn Ordâkhai tents ([see journal]/6)\tScouts ask that you destroy the tents and makeshift encampment the Ordâkhai have established beneath their large encampment in the crags south-east of Emax Dûl.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tWith the tents burned, you have surely set the Ordâkhai advance back. Find Mizâdi's scout, and return to the the encampment.\n",
[14909]="700744EE\n1\tDefeat the remaining Utûgi (total: 4)\030Defeat the remaining Ordâkhai (total: 10)\tMizâdi's forces want you to show no mercy. Hunt down the stragglers who wanted to escape to the south and grant them an ending fitting of such a terrible enemy.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tYou returned to the shore and found a small number of stragglers. After a quick foray into the marsh you emerged victorious. Now to find Mizâdi's scout and return to the encampment.\n",
[14910]="700744EF\n1\tFree the captive harvesters (total: 10)\tPleas of assistance to rescue more families forced into service by the Ordâkhai reach you. Beneath the shattered bridge to the south-east, more await release from their shackles.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tThe harvesters are free. Return to the road and speak with the scout to return to Mizâdi's encampment.\n",
[14911]="700744F0\n1\tDefeat Utûgi stragglers (total: 4)\030Defeat Ordâkhai warriors (total: 12)\tIt is unclear if the forces of Utûgi and Ordâkhai in the south-west of the Hatokáli Fells intend to attack or to flee across the river. It matters little to Mizâdi's scouts. They want the threat eliminated.\n2\tFind Mizâdi's scout\tYou have defeated a large number of Ordâkhai and Utûgi. Find Mizâdi's scout to return to the encampment.\n",
[14912]="700744F1\n1\tComplete the mission: Discovering Intent\tMizâdi's scouts are being cautious to deter any potential Ordâkhai footholds from being established any further within Hatokáli. You have been asked to stop a plot to retake the town lost when the Ordâkhai lost control of the scorpions.\n2\tComplete the mission: The Crates Are Empty...\tYour caution in retrieving the orders from the courier at the Ordâkhai encampment affords Mizâdi's forces an opportunity they had not expected; infiltration. You must not waste this opportunity to further hamper the Ordâkhai forces.\n3\tComplete the mission: Weaken Their Position\tMizâdi's infiltrator escaped while you destroyed the crates the Ordâkhai brought to their makeshift camp. As they fled, they saw that the Ordâkhai were not deterred. In fact, they returned from the crags with tents to make a more formidable forward camp.\n4\tSpeak with Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp\tYou destroyed the tents the Ordâkhai meant to use as shelter in the coming night. Perhaps this will be enough to stop their advance. You should return to Kusâg at Mizâdi's camp and speak with her.\n",
})
